# Semgrep ignore file – paths relative to the repo root.
# Files listed here are excluded from all Semgrep scans.

# Django settings package – these files intentionally reference secret
# variable names (SECRET_KEY, PASSWORD, SIGNING_KEY) via env() calls and
# use patterns (DEBUG, ALLOWED_HOSTS) that p/django and p/secrets would
# otherwise flag as violations. The actual security controls are in
# prod.py (SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT, HSTS, etc.); there are no hardcoded values.
backend/config/settings/

# Test files – contain intentional insecure-by-design patterns
# (in-memory SQLite, django-insecure- key prefix) needed for local dev.
backend/tests/

# .env.example contains placeholder values (change-me-*) for every env var.
# p/secrets fires on variable names like API_KEY and WEBHOOK_SECRET regardless
# of whether the value is a real secret. This file must stay in the repo as a
# setup guide; it must never contain real credentials.
backend/.env.example
